755	/// Perf finding: adapters were calling `PricingTable::seed()` fresh on every single
756	/// `parse_stream` invocation instead of reusing one shared instance, even though
757	/// `TokenEconomics::calculate` takes `&PricingTable` specifically so callers could avoid that.
758	/// `pricing::SEEDED` is a `LazyLock<PricingTable>` built once and reused. This test proves the
759	/// shared static is a behaviorally identical drop-in for a fresh `PricingTable::seed()` call --
760	/// the actual safety property worth testing, since "was an allocation avoided" isn't practically
761	/// testable without a dedicated allocation-counting harness.
